# Hackathon Kit config. No secrets here: keys live in .env (gitignored).
# scripts/init fills this in; edit by hand any time and commit it.
KIT_EVENT=""          # event name
KIT_REPO=""           # owner/name. Empty = read it from the git remote
KIT_LEAD=""           # GitHub login of the team lead. Empty = the repo owner
KIT_START=""          # local time building starts, YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM
KIT_DEADLINE=""       # local time of the hard submission deadline, YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM
KIT_LOG_ISSUE="1"     # number of the live-log issue
KIT_ACK_MIN="10"      # minutes before a directive nobody acked is flagged to the lead
KIT_BUDGET_USD=""     # team budget for paid APIs, if there is one
KIT_NOTIFY="1"        # 1 = scripts/watch also shows a desktop notification (macOS)

# Gates: percent of the build window | what must be true by then.
# Miss a gate: cut scope, don't slip. scripts/clock shows the times.
KIT_GATES="
5|Submission facts filled in docs/SUBMISSION.md; every agent ran scripts/catchup; lanes claimed
15|Idea picked by spike test (docs/IDEAS.md) and written in docs/DECISIONS.md
25|docs/DEMO.md written; golden path defined in scripts/check; shared formats frozen
45|Golden path runs end to end on main (mock data is fine)
65|Real results on main; every number in docs/EVIDENCE.md
80|FEATURE FREEZE: only fixes, README, demo and slides from here
90|Submission built by a script from a fresh clone; the organizers' checker passes
95|Submitted. Rehearse the talk twice with a timer
"
